---
// Ported from the Claude Design canvas artboard CaseGameUI.dc.html. Edit the canvas, then re-port.
import BaseV2 from '../../layouts/BaseV2.astro';
---
<BaseV2 title="Game UI Kits · Paramore.Design" description="Zelda, Satisfactory and Raid Rush rebuilt as Figma UI kits.">
  <!-- BLOCK: Case hero -->
  <section class="pd-wrap" data-screen-label="Hero">
    <div class="pd-topline">
      <a href="/work" style="text-decoration: none">← All projects</a>
      <span style="color: var(--color-accent-ink)">Personal Work // Game UI Studies</span>
    </div>
    <h1 class="pd-title" style="margin-top: 40px">Game UI Kits</h1>
    <div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-end; gap: 24px 48px; margin: 28px 0 40px">
      <p class="pd-lede">Game UI explorations and kits: Zelda: Breath of the Wild, Satisfactory, and Raid Rush. The Zelda kit was featured on the Figma community homepage.</p>
      <a href="https://www.figma.com/@hparamore" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="pd-btn pd-btn--primary">View on Figma →</a>
    </div>
    <!-- BLOCK: Meta strip -->
    <div class="pd-meta">
      <div><span class="pd-meta__label">Role</span><span class="pd-meta__value">Solo Designer</span></div>
      <div><span class="pd-meta__label">Discipline</span><span class="pd-meta__value">UI Design · Visual Systems</span></div>
      <div><span class="pd-meta__label">Tools</span><span class="pd-meta__value">Figma</span></div>
      <div><span class="pd-meta__label">Format</span><span class="pd-meta__value">UI Kits · HUD · Menus</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- BLOCK: Hero image -->
  <section class="pd-wrap" style="margin-top: 48px" data-screen-label="Hero image">
    <div class="pd-frame"><img src="/assets/images/projects/GameDesignSystem.jpg" alt="Zelda, Satisfactory and Raid Rush UI kits in Figma" style="aspect-ratio: 1252 / 1102; max-height: 820px"></div>
  </section>

  <!-- BLOCK: Text section -->
  <section class="pd-wrap pd-section" data-screen-label="Intro">
    <div class="pd-text" style="border-top: var(--pd-rule)">
      <div><div class="pd-kicker pd-kicker--accent" style="margin-bottom: 16px">Why games</div><h2 class="pd-h2">UI is loudest in games.</h2></div>
      <div class="pd-body" style="font-size: 17px">
        <p>Game UI lives in the hardest spot in design: it has to communicate fast, sit inside a living world, and never break the spell. These are personal studies of three very different games, rebuilt in Figma to understand how each one solves that problem.</p>
        <p>Each kit is a complete component library (type, color, iconography, HUD states, menu flows) published on my Figma community profile for anyone to fork or learn from.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- BLOCK: Kit (text + gallery) -->
  <section class="pd-wrap pd-section" data-screen-label="Zelda">
    <div class="pd-text" style="border-top: var(--pd-rule)">
      <div><div class="pd-kicker pd-kicker--accent" style="margin-bottom: 16px">Nintendo Switch</div><h2 class="pd-h2">Zelda <span class="pd-accent">Breath of the Wild</span></h2></div>
      <p class="pd-body" style="font-size: 17px">A study of one of the most quietly confident UI systems ever shipped: restrained color, generous negative space, and iconography that feels carved rather than drawn. The kit covers the pause menu, inventory, map, runes, and shrine UI.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pd-gallery" style="margin-top: 40px">
      <div class="pd-placeholder" style="aspect-ratio: 16 / 10">[Zelda kit screen 1]</div>
      <div class="pd-placeholder" style="aspect-ratio: 16 / 10">[Zelda kit screen 2]</div>
      <div class="pd-placeholder" style="aspect-ratio: 16 / 10">[Zelda kit screen 3]</div>
      <div class="pd-placeholder" style="aspect-ratio: 16 / 10">[Zelda kit screen 4]</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- BLOCK: Kit (text + gallery) -->
  <section class="pd-wrap pd-section" data-screen-label="Satisfactory">
    <div class="pd-text" style="border-top: var(--pd-rule)">
      <div><div class="pd-kicker pd-kicker--accent" style="margin-bottom: 16px">PC</div><h2 class="pd-h2">Satis<span class="pd-accent">factory</span></h2></div>
      <p class="pd-body" style="font-size: 17px">A factory-builder lives or dies by its UI: players spend hours inside menus, build trees, and production graphs. This kit reconstructs Satisfactory’s industrial, schematic-style interface: build menus, the MAM tree, AWESOME shop, and HUD readouts.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pd-gallery" style="margin-top: 40px">
      <div class="pd-placeholder" style="aspect-ratio: 16 / 10">[Satisfactory kit screen 1]</div>
      <div class="pd-placeholder" style="aspect-ratio: 16 / 10">[Satisfactory kit screen 2]</div>
      <div class="pd-placeholder" style="aspect-ratio: 16 / 10">[Satisfactory kit screen 3]</div>
      <div class="pd-placeholder" style="aspect-ratio: 16 / 10">[Satisfactory kit screen 4]</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- BLOCK: Kit (text + gallery, portrait) -->
  <section class="pd-wrap pd-section" data-screen-label="Raid Rush">
    <div class="pd-text" style="border-top: var(--pd-rule)">
      <div><div class="pd-kicker pd-kicker--accent" style="margin-bottom: 16px">Mobile</div><h2 class="pd-h2">Raid <span class="pd-accent">Rush</span></h2></div>
      <p class="pd-body" style="font-size: 17px">A mobile RPG UI kit: character screens, gear loadouts, raid queues, and the relentless economy of menus that mobile games run on. Built as a complete component set so the visual language stays consistent across every surface.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pd-gallery pd-gallery--phones" style="margin-top: 40px">
      <div class="pd-placeholder" style="aspect-ratio: 9 / 16">[Raid Rush screen 1]</div>
      <div class="pd-placeholder" style="aspect-ratio: 9 / 16">[Raid Rush screen 2]</div>
      <div class="pd-placeholder" style="aspect-ratio: 9 / 16">[Raid Rush screen 3]</div>
      <div class="pd-placeholder" style="aspect-ratio: 9 / 16">[Raid Rush screen 4]</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- BLOCK: Closing CTA -->
  <section class="pd-wrap pd-section pd-section--last" data-screen-label="Closing">
    <div class="pd-quote">
      <p class="pd-quote__text">Want the <span class="pd-accent">files?</span></p>
      <p class="pd-body" style="margin-top: 20px">Every kit is published on my Figma community profile, free to duplicate, fork, or rip apart for your own work.</p>
      <div class="pd-btns" style="margin-top: 28px">
        <a href="https://www.figma.com/@hparamore" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="pd-btn pd-btn--primary">View on Figma →</a>
        <a href="/work" class="pd-btn">More work</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- BLOCK: Next project -->
  <section class="pd-poster" data-screen-label="Next project">
    <div class="pd-poster__inner" style="padding-block: clamp(40px, 6vw, 72px)">
      <a href="/projects/mutual" class="pd-next">
        <div><div class="pd-kicker" style="margin-bottom: 16px">Next project</div><div class="pd-poster__title" style="font-size: clamp(44px, 6vw, 88px)">Mutual</div></div>
        <span class="pd-next__box" aria-hidden="true"><svg width="30" height="30" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="square"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"></path></svg></span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseV2>
